<speak>Yes, and I do not have to arrange the journey to the branch. I do not mind visiting when there is a practical reason, but the travelling can turn a short meeting into the main activity of the day. If it rains, I end up watching the weather and deciding whether to leave earlier. Then I worry about getting there too early and sitting around. At home I can make tea, put the papers out, and be ready without all that extra planning.</speak>